{"comment":"The page entry of air-ide: one port on 127.0.0.1 that answers the host document and the WebSocket of the host page. The step httpRequest {method, path, host, origin, expect, headers?, body?} sends one HTTP request without an upgrade to 127.0.0.1:${port} and expects the status, the headers by their lowercase names and the exact body; null for origin sends no Origin header. The step wsHandshake {origin, host, expect} opens a WebSocket to ws://127.0.0.1:${port}/ with these headers and expects the HTTP status. Each later line of the link page is one text frame of the last WebSocket that opened, and a line with binary one binary frame. A line of the link ide with conn 2 is on a second connection of air-ide, by the order of its initialize. The step wsClose {closeCode} expects air-ide to close it, or closes it from the page. The step pageLoad {url, location} is the load of the host document in the browser of a view and the address of the page after it, and pageTicket {ticket} the call window.airAppHost.connect(ticket) of the IDE in the main frame of that browser; a runner of air-ide skips both."}
